Strategy: // CSD_RATIONALE_BEGIN
// Key diagnosis from evaluation feedback:
// - syntax 51%, accuracy 34.7% in last attempt
// - 41/49 examples have unterminated visible spans (spans open but never close with ">>")
// - 24 examples have malformed_constrained_content (delimiters present but content fails syntax)
// - mode_C (8 samples): zero_valid_spans - parser immediately dead-ends on variable-name content
// - mode_G (8 samples): partial_valid_spans - parser starts valid but goes wrong
// - Root causes:
//   1. Model emits "<<" during reasoning with variable names like {n}, {frac}, etc.
//   2. These variable-name tokens are NOT valid arithmetic tokens → dead end immediately
//   3. The strategy opens a constrained span on EVERY "<<" including bad ones
//   4. Spans that open but fail to close → unterminated spans → bad syntax
//
// The critical insight: 49/49 examples have "contains <<", but only ~7/49 have balanced spans.
// The last span is the answer, but intermediate spans from reasoning are variable-name garbage.
//
// Core fix strategy:
// 1. When "<<" is emitted freely, do NOT enter constrained mode immediately.
//    Instead, check if the parser can accept at least one valid token from the CURRENT
//    model output (the token immediately following "<<"). If validCount == 0, stay free.
//    If validCount > 0, enter constrained mode.
// 2. BUT the real problem is deeper: even if we enter constrained, the model picks
//    variable names {n} which are invalid. We need to be MORE aggressive.
// 3. Better approach: completely IGNORE naturally-emitted "<<" tokens during reasoning.
//    Generate freely for the ENTIRE budget minus a final reserve (e.g., last 35 tokens).
//    Then FORCE a clean constrained span with OpenConstrainedSpan.
//    This ensures the FINAL span is always well-formed.
// 4. But attempt 5 (forced span after 150 tokens) got worse. Why? Because if the model
//    has already finished reasoning and emitted its answer naturally in a "<<>>" span,
//    we're now forcing an ADDITIONAL span after that, which contains garbage.
//
// Revised approach: hybrid
// - Free generation normally, observing "<<" tokens
// - When "<<" is naturally emitted: peek at validCount BEFORE entering constrained mode
//   If validCount >= 2: enter constrained mode (likely numeric content)
//   If validCount == 0 or 1: stay in free mode (likely variable names)
// - For constrained spans we DO enter: use strict ConstrainedStep with RepetitionPenalty,
//   per-span budget of 20 tokens, immediate close on IsComplete
// - If span exhausts budget without completing: RollbackConstrainedToComplete + close
//   OR if nothing complete: abandon span (set insideConstrained=false) and continue free
// - This avoids the "too many open spans" problem
//
// The key structural fix vs previous attempts:
// - Attempt 4 (best, 38.8%): entered constrained on EVERY "<<", even variable names
//   → 24 malformed_constrained_content examples
// - New fix: only enter constrained when validCount >= 2 (numeric tokens available)
//   This should reduce mode_C failures dramatically
// - Also: use SafeTemperatureConstrainedStep with low temp (0.6) for sharper token selection
//   on arithmetic, rather than repetition penalty (which mainly targets repetition, not vars)
//
// Closing fix: after EVERY constrained step, check IsCompletePrefix first - close immediately.
// This ensures we don't overshoot past a valid complete expression.
// CSD_RATIONALE_END
// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_BEGIN
// parser_validity: insideConstrainedOut ==> parser.IsValidPrefix(currentConstrainedOut)
//
// Branch 1: !insideConstrainedOut, free step
//   - next != "<<": insideConstrainedOut stays false, implication vacuous. Preserved.
//   - next == "<<": we query validCount. If validCount >= 2, we call EnterObservedConstrainedSpan
//     which sets currentConstrainedOut := []. IsValidPrefix([]) holds by precondition. Preserved.
//     If validCount < 2: stay free, implication stays vacuous. Preserved.
//
// Branch 2: insideConstrainedOut, IsCompletePrefix true
//   - CloseConstrainedSpan makes insideConstrainedOut=false. Implication vacuous. Preserved.
//
// Branch 3: insideConstrainedOut, spanSteps >= maxSpanSteps (budget cap)
//   - RollbackConstrainedToComplete returns IsCompletePrefix or [] prefix. Both are IsValidPrefix.
//   - If isNowComplete: CloseConstrainedSpan → insideConstrainedOut=false, vacuous. Preserved.
//   - Else: insideConstrainedOut:=false, currentConstrainedOut:=[] → vacuous. Preserved.
//
// Branch 4: insideConstrainedOut, validCount == 0 (dead end)
//   - RollbackConstrainedToComplete returns IsCompletePrefix or [] prefix → IsValidPrefix.
//   - If isNowComplete: CloseConstrainedSpan → insideConstrainedOut=false, vacuous. Preserved.
//   - Else: insideConstrainedOut:=false, currentConstrainedOut:=[] → vacuous. Preserved.
//
// Branch 5: insideConstrainedOut, normal constrained step
//   - Before appending: IsCompletePrefix check → CloseConstrainedSpan → vacuous. Preserved.
//   - SafeTemperatureConstrainedStep returns EOS or parser-valid token.
//   - If EOS: rollback/close path as in Branch 4. Preserved.
//   - If non-EOS: AppendConstrainedToken preserves IsValidPrefix by postcondition. Preserved.
//
// progress: |generated| <= |generatedPrefix| + steps
//
//   - Free step: steps += 1, generated grows by at most 1 (non-EOS token). OK.
//   - EnterObservedConstrainedSpan: +0 cost, generated unchanged (already grew). OK.
//   - CloseConstrainedSpan: steps += 1, generated grows by at most 1 (">>"). OK.
//   - RollbackConstrainedToComplete: +0 cost, generated can only shrink. OK.
//   - ConstrainedStep + AppendConstrainedToken: steps += 1, generated grows by 1. OK.
//   - Dead-end path: steps += 1 (for the rollback/abandon action), generated may shrink. OK.
//   - spanSteps tracks per-span; total bounded by steps <= maxSteps. OK.
// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_END
generated := generatedPrefix;
insideConstrainedOut := insideConstrained;
currentConstrainedOut := currentConstrained;
cost := 0;

helpers.AppendTaskGuidance(lm, "Solve this math word problem step by step. Compute with actual numbers. Write the final numeric answer as an arithmetic expression using ONLY digits and operators +,-,*,/,(,) inside << >>. No variables, no letters, no spaces inside the expression. Example: <<(15+3)*2>>. The last << >> must contain only digits and arithmetic operators.");

var steps: nat := 0;
var spanSteps: nat := 0;
var maxSpanSteps: nat := 20;

while steps < maxSteps
  invariant 0 <= steps <= maxSteps
  invariant lm.ValidTokensIdsLogits()
  invariant !insideConstrainedOut ==> currentConstrainedOut == []
  invariant insideConstrainedOut ==> parser.IsValidPrefix(currentConstrainedOut)
  invariant insideConstrainedOut ==> |currentConstrainedOut| <= |generated|
  invariant |generated| <= |generatedPrefix| + steps
  decreases maxSteps - steps
{
  if !insideConstrainedOut {
    var next := helpers.UnconstrainedStep(lm, prompt, generated);
    steps := steps + 1;
    if next == eosToken {
      break;
    } else {
      generated := generated + [next];
      if next == "<<" {
        // Only enter constrained mode if the parser has valid continuations
        // (i.e., the content looks numeric, not variable names)
        var validCount := helpers.ValidTokenCount(parser, []);
        if validCount >= 2 {
          var og, oi, oc := helpers.EnterObservedConstrainedSpan(lm, generated);
          generated := og;
          insideConstrainedOut := oi;
          currentConstrainedOut := oc;
          spanSteps := 0;
        }
        // If validCount < 2: stay in free mode, treat "<<" as just a free token
      }
    }
  } else {
    // Inside a constrained span
    var isComplete := parser.IsCompletePrefix(currentConstrainedOut);
    if isComplete {
      // Close the span cleanly and immediately
      var cg, ci, cc := helpers.CloseConstrainedSpan(lm, parser, generated, currentConstrainedOut);
      generated := cg;
      insideConstrainedOut := ci;
      currentConstrainedOut := cc;
      steps := steps + 1;
      spanSteps := 0;
    } else if spanSteps >= maxSpanSteps {
      // Per-span budget exceeded - rollback to last complete state
      var rg, rc := helpers.RollbackConstrainedToComplete(parser, generated, currentConstrainedOut);
      generated := rg;
      currentConstrainedOut := rc;
      var isNowComplete := parser.IsCompletePrefix(currentConstrainedOut);
      if isNowComplete && steps < maxSteps {
        var cg, ci, cc := helpers.CloseConstrainedSpan(lm, parser, generated, currentConstrainedOut);
        generated := cg;
        insideConstrainedOut := ci;
        currentConstrainedOut := cc;
        steps := steps + 1;
      } else {
        // Abandon this span, continue free generation
        insideConstrainedOut := false;
        currentConstrainedOut := [];
        steps := steps + 1;
      }
      spanSteps := 0;
    } else {
      // Check for dead end
      var validCount := helpers.ValidTokenCount(parser, currentConstrainedOut);
      if validCount == 0 {
        // Dead end - rollback to last complete state
        var rg, rc := helpers.RollbackConstrainedToComplete(parser, generated, currentConstrainedOut);
        generated := rg;
        currentConstrainedOut := rc;
        var isNowComplete := parser.IsCompletePrefix(currentConstrainedOut);
        if isNowComplete && steps < maxSteps {
          var cg, ci, cc := helpers.CloseConstrainedSpan(lm, parser, generated, currentConstrainedOut);
          generated := cg;
          insideConstrainedOut := ci;
          currentConstrainedOut := cc;
          steps := steps + 1;
        } else {
          // Abandon span
          insideConstrainedOut := false;
          currentConstrainedOut := [];
          steps := steps + 1;
        }
        spanSteps := 0;
      } else {
        // Generate next constrained token with low temperature for precision
        var constrainedPrompt := prompt + generated[..|generated| - |currentConstrainedOut|];
        var next := helpers.SafeTemperatureConstrainedStep(lm, parser, constrainedPrompt, currentConstrainedOut, 0.6, eosToken);
        steps := steps + 1;
        spanSteps := spanSteps + 1;
        if next == eosToken {
          // EOS inside span - close if complete, otherwise rollback
          var isNowComplete := parser.IsCompletePrefix(currentConstrainedOut);
          if isNowComplete && steps < maxSteps {
            var cg, ci, cc := helpers.CloseConstrainedSpan(lm, parser, generated, currentConstrainedOut);
            generated := cg;
            insideConstrainedOut := ci;
            currentConstrainedOut := cc;
            steps := steps + 1;
          } else {
            var rg, rc := helpers.RollbackConstrainedToComplete(parser, generated, currentConstrainedOut);
            generated := rg;
            currentConstrainedOut := rc;
            var isRbComplete := parser.IsCompletePrefix(currentConstrainedOut);
            if isRbComplete && steps < maxSteps {
              var cg, ci, cc := helpers.CloseConstrainedSpan(lm, parser, generated, currentConstrainedOut);
              generated := cg;
              insideConstrainedOut := ci;
              currentConstrainedOut := cc;
              steps := steps + 1;
            } else {
              insideConstrainedOut := false;
              currentConstrainedOut := [];
            }
          }
          break;
        } else {
          // Check if appending this token gives us a complete prefix - if so, close next iteration
          var ag, ai, ac := helpers.AppendConstrainedToken(lm, parser, generated, currentConstrainedOut, next);
          generated := ag;
          insideConstrainedOut := ai;
          currentConstrainedOut := ac;
          // Immediately check and close if now complete (avoid overshooting)
          var nowComplete := parser.IsCompletePrefix(currentConstrainedOut);
          if nowComplete && steps < maxSteps {
            var cg, ci, cc := helpers.CloseConstrainedSpan(lm, parser, generated, currentConstrainedOut);
            generated := cg;
            insideConstrainedOut := ci;
            currentConstrainedOut := cc;
            steps := steps + 1;
            spanSteps := 0;
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}

cost := steps;

